#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1125 expect=noViolation domain=VS
#note "Blank-key branch (D-TA-7a shape): the only record that deviates on --ELTM (PT2H against the group majority PT1H) leaves --TPT empty. What this arm pins is the GROUPING-KEY policy: is_inconsistent_across_dataset groups under GroupKeyPolicy.DROP_MISSING_KEYS (blankness = MISSING_OR_EMPTY), so a row whose --TPT key component is blank is dropped from grouping altogether and can never be flagged (GroupSemantics.group); the remaining two records agree. TA-6 (ruled 2026-08-19) DROPPED the provably-redundant `not empty(--TPT)` / `not empty(--ELTM)` conjuncts from the SD1125 twins — this arm's verdict is unchanged by the drop, exactly as the mechanical lane's measurement predicted (findings-diff zero)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset VS class=FINDINGS label="Vital Signs"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VSTPTREF type=Char label="Time Point Reference"
col VSTPTNUM type=Num  label="Planned Time Point Number"
col VSTPT    type=Char label="Planned Time Point Name"
col VSELTM   type=Char label="Planned Elapsed Time from Time Point Ref"
---
S1 | VS | 001 | 1 | SYSBP | 1 | DOSE | 1 | 1H POST | PT1H
S1 | VS | 002 | 1 | SYSBP | 1 | DOSE | 1 | 1H POST | PT1H
S1 | VS | 003 | 1 | SYSBP | 1 | DOSE | 1 |         | PT2H
